*   **style_sleek_vs_boxy**: 0.50. The TT has an iconic, sleek coupe design with flowing lines (Source [2], [8], [13], [19], [28], [39]). This is on the sleeker side of the spectrum.
*   **style_aggression_rating**: 0.30. The TTS has sporty styling cues but is not as overtly aggressive as higher-performance sports cars or muscle cars. Score reflects a moderate level of aggression.
*   **style_modernity_rating**: 0.30. The TT's design is well-established but has received updates (Source [2], [8], [39]). It still looks modern, but isn't groundbreaking or avant-garde.
*   **handling_rating**: 0.60. The TTS is praised for its responsive handling, grip, and stability, making it confidence-inspiring, though some reviews find it less engaging than rivals like the Cayman (Source [2], [8], [16], [19], [20], [24], [25], [39]). It's well above average.
*   **ride_comfort_rating**: 0.40. The standard adaptive suspension (Audi Magnetic Ride) provides a balance between sportiness and comfort, making it reasonably comfortable for a sports car, especially in Comfort mode (Source [8], [16], [19], [20], [24], [25]). More comfortable than many direct sports car rivals.
*   **cabin_noise_rating**: 0.30. The TTS is noted as being relatively quiet for a sports coupe, without excessive wind or tire noise at speed, especially with the available Bang & Olufsen system (Source [8], [16], [27]). Above average.
*   **shift_smooth_rating**: 0.20. The seven-speed dual-clutch transmission is generally described as quick and smooth (Source [2], [8], [19], [24], [25], [26]).
*   **steering_feel_rating**: -0.20. While the steering is described as precise and responsive (Source [11], [12]), some reviews imply it might lack the ultimate engagement or feel of the best sports cars (Source [2], [8], [16], [19], [24], [25]). Slightly below the most engaging steering systems.
*   **adas_score**: 0.20. The TTS includes features like cruise control, parking sensors, reversing camera, lane departure warning, and blind-spot monitoring (available/standard depending on market/trim) (Source [8], [10], [17], [20], [32], [37], [38]). It offers a decent suite but lacks the most advanced semi-autonomous driving features.
*   **visibility_rating**: 0.30. The TT has fairly thin door pillars and a good view out for a sports coupe (Source [8], [10]).
*   **headlight_rating**: 0.30. LED headlights are standard (Source [8], [10], [18], [20], [25]). This is better than basic halogens, but not the most advanced matrix LED systems available (though Matrix LEDs were available on some TT models, Source [19], [28] in previous searches).
*   **security_rating**: 0.00. Standard security features include an anti-theft alarm and keyless entry (Source [8], [10], [18], [20], [32]). No specific data on advanced security features like trackers was found, so an average score is assigned.
*   **screen_in**: 0.40. The TTS features a 12.3-inch Audi Virtual Cockpit digital driver's display (Source [5], [8], [10], [19], [20], [23], [27], [33], [38]). This is larger than the average infotainment screen size.
*   **infotainment_ux_rating**: 0.60. The Audi Virtual Cockpit is praised for its high resolution, customizability, and ease of use, integrating navigation and media well, despite the lack of a central touchscreen (Source [5], [8], [10], [19], [20], [23], [25], [27]).
*   **smartphone_connect_rating**: 0.20. Apple CarPlay and Android Auto are standard (Source [2], [8], [10], [20], [27], [32], [38]). Wireless phone charging is also available (Source [8], [10]). Some sources indicate a wired connection is required for CarPlay/Android Auto (Source [9]). This is good, but not the best (which would include wireless CarPlay/AA standard).
*   **audio_rating**: 0.50. The Bang & Olufsen sound system is available or standard on higher TTS trims (Source [11], [27], [32], [34], [38]). This is a premium audio system, well above average.
*   **usb_ports**: 0.00. The number of USB ports was not specified in the search results. An average score is assigned.
*   **comfort_feature_score**: 0.40. Features like heated front Super Sport seats (leather/Alcantara or Nappa leather), power seats, and dual-zone automatic climate control are standard or available (Source [1], [2], [3], [4], [5], [6], [8], [9], [11], [14], [16], [18], [20], [21], [22], [32], [34], [36], [38]). This provides a good level of comfort features for a sports car.
*   **convenience_feature_score**: 0.20. Features like keyless entry/go, cruise control, light/rain sensors, parking sensors, and a reversing camera are available or standard (Source [2], [3], [5], [7], [8], [10], [11], [14], [16], [17], [18], [20], [22], [32], [38]). It lacks some of the more advanced convenience features found in larger luxury vehicles (e.g., 360 cameras, remote park).
